vendored: 2026-08-05

Why vendored rather than loaded from a CDN
------------------------------------------

Until 2026-08-05 `base.html` loaded this file from `unpkg.com` at render
time, unpinned and without an integrity attribute. Two problems:

1. **It made the console depend on the *viewer's* internet access.** vq
   consoles are typically reached over a private overlay on fleets that
   may have no egress at all. Without htmx the page still renders and
   still looks correct — but nothing refreshes, and every button driven
   by `hx-post` silently does nothing. A dashboard that stops updating
   without saying so is worse than one that fails.
2. **It put an unpinned third-party script in the trust path of a
   surface that can kill jobs.** The console's write actions are one
   `hx-post` away.

0BSD grants redistribution outright with no attribution condition, so
vendoring carries no obligation beyond this record (CLAUDE.md § 1).

Re-fetching / upgrading
-----------------------

    curl -fsSL -o htmx.min.js https://unpkg.com/htmx.org@<version>/dist/htmx.min.js
    shasum -a 256 htmx.min.js      # then update this file

Check the upstream changelog for breaking changes first: the console
relies on `hx-get`, `hx-post`, `hx-trigger`, `hx-swap` and `hx-target`,
and on htmx 2.x's behaviour of NOT swapping non-2xx responses (which is
what makes an expired session leave the last-good fragment on screen
instead of painting a login form into a table).
